Author: LstDtchMn <nlsurfer@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 24 06:55:03 2026 -0400

    M19-1/M19-2: evidence identity is a revision, not a name
    
    A stable name cannot be the durable identity of evidence. Two request
    definitions can be published under one arm deliberately, and keying the
    ledger on the name lets the second refresh the first's rows, merge their
    sightings and dates, and destroy which definition made which claim. A
    contract that correctly refuses the second cannot repair evidence already
    aggregated across both.
    
    Identity is now (arm_id, request_definition_version, parser_version).
    
    M19-1 -- backend/arms.py rewritten
      - arm_id is OPAQUE and uses dots, not colons, so code still splitting on
        the round-19 separator fails loudly instead of returning a wrong answer.
        A static guard greps the backend for exactly that.
      - request_definition_version is a digest of the canonical request, stored
        WITH its preimage: a digest nobody can check is not auditable.
      - Pagination is declared data, not code. There are FOUR branches, not two:
        adit-hd DROPS the query suffix on page N, so two feeds identical in path
        and query are not the same request. A test rebuilds every page URL from
        the declared form and compares it to the crawler's own construction.
      - The registry refuses four ways to collapse two feeds into one identity,
        not one: duplicate id, one request under two names, a legacy key claimed
        by two arms, and a legacy key equal to a live id.
      - An undeclared feed gets a deterministic arm.unregistered.* id rather
        than raising. It records sightings and can never support a proof; a
        crawl must not die because a feed was added and not declared.
    
    M19-2 -- migration split in two, by risk
      - SHAPE (automatic): widen the key. Invents nothing -- the legacy key is
        carried across verbatim and both version columns are left EMPTY, which
        is the durable marker for "never attributed".
      - ATTRIBUTION (gated, DRY-RUN BY DEFAULT): decide which arm and revision a
        row belongs to, or quarantine it. Every decision is audited, including
        the ones that change nothing.
      - Plan and apply share ONE transaction. The previous version read in one
        and wrote in another, so a concurrent writer could add rows under a key
        already classified and they would be missed with no record.
      - posted_date_raw is MERGED, not dropped. The old merge never mentioned
        it, so one row's date silently won and the other was destroyed; a
        disagreement is now recorded as a change instead of discarded with the
        losing value. Ordering uses julianday(), never a string compare -- a
        same-day mix of 'T' and ' ' separators inverts the comparison.
    
    Quarantine does NOT remove the row from the ledger. Unattributable evidence
    may narrow authority but never widen it: a row whose arm is unknown can
    still contradict a claim, and deleting it removes that contradiction, which
    makes a negative claim easier to sustain. That is widening by omission.
    
    Verified against a VACUUM INTO copy of the deployed database, not synthetic
    data. All 266 live rows migrate shape-only with none lost or altered,
    nothing attributed, idempotent, user_version still 9. Attribution resolves
    all three live keys (tv 105, 4k 93, remux 68). Atomicity is proven by
    behaviour: an injected failure two thirds through discarded all 161 rows
    already written -- sqlite in autocommit would make rollback a silent no-op
    while the docstring still claimed atomicity.
    
    70 new tests. The two round-19 test files are retired: they assert the
    superseded colon-key shape and cannot pass. Every intent that still holds
    is carried forward. The round-16 crawl harness was building a made-up feed
    URL, so tests using it were unknowingly running against an unregistered
    arm; it now uses the real declared feeds.
    
    Full suite 11 failed / 5568 passed. All 11 fail at HEAD too (8 clicknload,
    1 dv_settings, 2 auto-resume) and are unrelated to this change.
    
    Not deployed. Live apply remains gated.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

